
THREE RULES to remember befor applying two pointers: 

Rule 1: Sorted data

Two pointers usually require sorted input.

Rule 2: One pointer moves at a time

Movement is logical, not random.

Rule 3: Stop condition

Usually:

while left < right



Common begginner mistakes to avoid: 

Forgetting array must be sorted

Moving both pointers blindly

Using <= instead of <

Trying two pointers where hashing is better